<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cutter carcasses steady; Utility carcasses not established. Demand and offerings moderate.</p>
<p>- USDA.</p>
<p>COW &amp; BULL CARCASS FOB OMAHA	  5.0   Loads Reported.</p>
<p>			  Lds   Price Range    Latest Estb. Mkt.</p>
<p>UT,brk 2-4 450#/up				  48.50 A</p>
<p>UT,bng 1-3 400#/up				  52.50 A</p>
<p>Cutter 1-2 350#/up  5.0   53.00		 53.00</p>
<p>Bulls YG 1 500#/up				  unq</p>
<p>BONELESS PROCESSING BEEF/BEEF TRIMMINGS   46.0  Loads Reported.</p>
<p>Boneless processing beef steady in the Midwest, while lean boneless beef in Texas traded $1.50-2.00 higher. Demand and offerings moderate. Beef trimmings higher on light demand and offerings.</p>
